{"name":"Deep Ultramarine","hex":"#404f95","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.\nExtending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively.","Extending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"},{"term":"ultramarine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Beyond the sea.","Of a brilliant dark blue or slightly purplish color like that of the pigment (noun sense 1)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In full ultramarine blue: a brilliant blue pigment traditionally made from ground-up lapis lazuli, and now usually either extracted from mineral deposits or made synthetically.","A brilliant dark blue or slightly purplish colour like that of the pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ultramarine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ultramarine","blocks":[{"text":"Ultramarine is a deep blue pigment historically derived from lazurite, the principal component of the metamorphic rock lapis lazuli. The pigment was produced by grinding the stone and undergoing a complex washing process to isolate the blue mineral, which made it exceptionally valuable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ultramarinepigment.jpg/330px-Ultramarinepigment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultramarine"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Natural_ultramarine_painted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikiped